{"entity":{"id":"hb:pagan@1279","name":"Pagan","dataset":"basemaps","kind":"polity"},"territories":[{"id":2186,"name":"Pagan","set_id":"hb_1279","class":"kingdom","valid_from":1279,"valid_to":1300,"snapshot_held":1,"area_km2":732231.7034211871,"border_precision":1,"capital_name":null,"sovereign":null,"sovereign_note":null,"modern_name":"Myanmar (Burma)","min_lon":91.41017440269734,"min_lat":15.677930437285326,"max_lon":101.00763564981274,"max_lat":25.97602530564657,"source_file":"world_1279.geojson","source_row":null},{"id":2300,"name":"Pagan","set_id":"hb_1300","class":"polity","valid_from":1300,"valid_to":1400,"snapshot_held":1,"area_km2":732231.7034211871,"border_precision":1,"capital_name":null,"sovereign":null,"sovereign_note":null,"modern_name":"Myanmar (Burma)","min_lon":91.41017440269734,"min_lat":15.677930437285326,"max_lon":101.00763564981274,"max_lat":25.97602530564657,"source_file":"world_1300.geojson","source_row":null},{"id":2410,"name":"Pagan","set_id":"hb_1400","class":"polity","valid_from":1400,"valid_to":1492,"snapshot_held":1,"area_km2":732231.7034211871,"border_precision":1,"capital_name":null,"sovereign":null,"sovereign_note":null,"modern_name":"Myanmar (Burma)","min_lon":91.41017440269734,"min_lat":15.677930437285326,"max_lon":101.00763564981274,"max_lat":25.97602530564657,"source_file":"world_1400.geojson","source_row":null}],"identities":[{"qid":"Q888574","from_t":1279,"to_t":1297.978082191781,"method":"name-template+date","confidence":0.8673231417419456,"label":"Pagan kingdom","description":"former country","inception":849.9753424657534,"dissolved":1297.958904109589,"enwiki":"Pagan Kingdom","summary":"The Pagan Kingdom (Burmese: ပုဂံပြည် Băgam pyi [bəɡàɰ̃ pji]; lit. 'Bagan state'), also called Bagan Empire (ပုဂံဧကရာဇ်နိုင်ငံတော်) or the First Burmese Empire, was the first Burmese kingdom to unify the regions that would later constitute modern-day Myanmar. Pagan's 250-year rule over the Irrawaddy valley and its periphery laid the foundation for the ascent of Burmese language and culture, the spread of Bamar ethnicity in Upper Myanmar, and the growth of Theravada Buddhism in Myanmar and in mainland Southeast Asia.\nThe kingdom grew out of a small 9th-century settlement at Pagan by the Mranma people, the predecessor to the modern Bamar ethnicity. Over the next two hundred years, the small principality gradually grew to absorb its surrounding regions until the 1050s and 1060s when King Anawrahta founded the Pagan Empire, presumably for the first time unifying under one polity the Irrawaddy valley and its periphery."}],"facts":[{"qid":"Q888574","kind":"capital","value_qid":"Q29317","value_label":"Bagan","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P36","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Bagan"},{"qid":"Q888574","kind":"official_religion","value_qid":"Q748","value_label":"Buddhism","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P3075","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Buddhism"},{"qid":"Q888574","kind":"government","value_qid":"Q7269","value_label":"monarchy","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P122","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"monarchy"}],"people":{},"media":{},"names":["Dinastia Bagan","Dinastia Pagan","Dinastia de Pagan","Eerste Birmaanse koninkrijk","First Burmese Empire","Império de Pagan","Królestwo Paganu","Königreich von Bagan","Pagan","Pagan Krallığı","Pagan kingdom","Regno Pagan","Reino de Bagan","Reino de Pagan","royaume de Pagan","Βασίλειο του Παγκάν","Паганское царство","مملكة باغان","پادشاهی پاگان","बगान साम्राज्य","パガン朝","パガン王朝","夫甘都卢","夫甘都卢国","蒲甘","蒲甘王國","蒲甘王朝"]}